{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791051285,"nonce":"W3nUCqZdGEQJ6i9nHTVfpbVO2pE=","title":"Monomorphizer: body-only type parameters and generics called from generics are trap-stubbed","message":"Found vendoring the Haxe 5 haxe.runtime.Copy (Issue12538 behind it; Issue11863 passes through a path that avoids it).\n\n- `copyValue\u003cT, O:{} \u0026 T\u003e(v:T):T` declares `O`, used only in its body (`var v:O = cast v`). Calls carry one explicit type argument for two parameters (`[mono] copyValue EXPLICIT type_args=[Ptr(Void)]`) and the template is not specialised.\n- `getRef\u003cT:{}\u003e(v:T)` is called from inside the generic `copyValue` with `v:O`: the call's argument type is the OUTER template's parameter, so `[mono] getRef NO explicit type_args; type_params=[\"T\"] param_tys=[Ptr(Void), I64]` cannot infer T (\"no TypeVar param matches\": the template params are already erased).\n- `copy\u003cT\u003e(v:T):T` itself then stubs (`[trap-stub:generic] copy/copyValue/getRef`) and main cascades.\n\nNeeded in ir/monomorphize.rs: a type parameter with no binding at a call (body-only, or unresolvable) specialises as Dynamic/erased instead of skipping; a call inside a template whose argument types are the template's own parameters is re-resolved when the enclosing template is specialised.\n\nProbe: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-amaterasu-Vibranium-rayzor/0e5285ee-bd3c-4d54-a191-d5a96a4ca7c6/scratchpad/probe/bnd2 (`haxe.runtime.Copy.copy(new P(3))`).","files":null}]}